My study approach
Time invested: ~45 hours over [3 weeks]
What I actually did:

Handwritten notes on every domain — writing by hand forced me to process the material instead of just reading it
Built mental models for abstract concepts (shared responsibility, global infrastructure, pricing) before memorizing details
Focused on why each service exists, not just what it does

What clicked for me:
The exam is less about remembering service names and more about understanding when you'd choose one thing over another. Knowing that Lambda is for short-lived event-driven tasks versus EC2 for persistent workloads matters more than recalling specific limits.
